 "_source": {
  "description": "DQN learning curves of the MinAtar paper, read off the published figure; the paper releases no numeric results. Each point is the moving average of return over the last 100 training episodes, averaged over 30 runs, at the step size that gave the best final return for the game. The agent uses RMSprop, Huber loss and all 6 actions, over 5M frames with no frame skip. Values are digitized from the plot's pixels and are accurate to about half a percent of the axis height; every point is the mean of the trace within 0.05M steps. Seaquest is omitted since it is not supported here.",
  "citation": "Young and Tian, \"MinAtar: An Atari-Inspired Testbed for Thorough and Reproducible Reinforcement Learning Experiments\", 2019 (https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.03176)",
